e}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000188818","entrez_id":["79844"],"uniprot":["Q9H8X9"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables signaling adaptor activity. Involved in antiviral innate immune response and positive regulation of defense response to virus by host. Located in endoplasmic reticulum. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9H8X9","text":"Endoplasmic reticulum-localized palmitoyltransferase that could catalyze the addition of palmitate onto various protein substrates and be involved in a variety of cellular processes (By similarity). Has a palmitoyltransferase activity toward NCDN and regulates NCDN association with endosome membranes through this palmitoylation (By similarity). May play a role in cell proliferation (PubMed:28331227). Also has a palmitoyltransferase activity-independent function in DNA virus-triggered and CGAS-mediated innate immune response (PubMed:28331227). Functions as an adapter that recruits IRF3 to STING1 to promote the activation of that key transcriptional regulator of type I interferon (IFN)-dependent immune response (PubMed:28331227)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}